WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.652
This query joins patients with admissions.

00:00:02.652 --> 00:00:08.697
The name is trimmed, repeated whitespace is collapsed, and display case is applied.

00:00:08.697 --> 00:00:12.657
The email domain is extracted from a normalized email.

00:00:12.657 --> 00:00:15.552
Admission time is reduced to month grain.

00:00:15.552 --> 00:00:18.967
Length of stay is converted to numeric days.

00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:23.437
Read the query column by column rather than as one large block.

00:00:23.437 --> 00:00:29.192
Connect this idea to an operations team aligning timestamps across locations.

00:00:29.192 --> 00:00:34.562
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:34.562 --> 00:00:42.122
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:42.122 --> 00:00:47.397
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:47.397 --> 00:00:52.880
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
